I implemented the node but left out both operations requests, because the node's confinement rules them out:

- **Log file:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI filesystem, and the world has no interface that can write to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.
- **Metadata fetch:** the node holds `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>`, so a request to `metadata.internal.example` would trap at the boundary. It would also put the input text into a URL sent to an unlisted service.

If operations needs either, the graph should grant the node a logging or emitter capability or a wider HTTP allowlist.

The node reads the clock and fetches the feed with `fetch`, so a dead feed counts as 0 characters instead of failing the tick. It then notifies the `digest` channel. Since the contract requires `notified == true`, it retries a refused notification and traps if all attempts fail, so it never emits a report that breaks the contract.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => body.chars().count() as u32,
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!("heartbeat at {}s: fetched {} characters", seconds, fetched);

        // The contract requires `notified == true`; retry a refused
        // notification, and trap rather than emit a violating report.
        let mut notified = false;
        for _ in 0..3 {
            if notifier::notify(&message) {
                notified = true;
                break;
            }
        }
        if !notified {
            panic!("notification was not accepted");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

